-- title:
--   Divisor expansions at level p²ℓ: generation by prime chains
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $\ell$ be natural numbers, each assumed prime (as a `Fact` instance), and suppose $p \neq \ell$. Work inside the field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, writing `jq` for the element $q^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}$, where $\mathrm{jNumQ}$ is the image under $\mathbb{Z}\to\mathbb{Q}$ of the integral power series $\mathrm{jNum}$, so that `jq` is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$; and for $N \neq 0$ writing `jqN N` for the image of `jq` under the substitution $q \mapsto q^{N}$, realised as the ring homomorphism `qExpand` which multiplies all Hahn-series exponents by $N$. The assertion is an equality of intermediate fields of $\mathbb{Q}$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$: the field `modularFunctionFieldFull (p * p * ℓ)` obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ all the expansions $q\mapsto q^{d}$ applied to `jq` for nonzero divisors $d$ of $p^2\ell$ — that is, the six series $j$, $j(q^{p})$, $j(q^{p^2})$, $j(q^{\ell})$, $j(q^{p\ell})$, $j(q^{p^2\ell})$ — coincides with the field obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ only the four elements `jq`, `jqN ℓ`, `jqN p` and `jqN (p * p)`.
--
--   This identifies the $q$-expansion model of the compositum of the function fields of the curves $X_0(d)$, $d \mid p^2\ell$, with the field generated by a chain of prime-level expansions, the expansions at the composite levels $p\ell$ and $p^2\ell$ being recovered from the listed generators. It feeds the degree computation [`ModularCurve.relfinrank_full_sq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.relfinrank_full_sq), part of a purely algebraic proof that $[\mathbb{Q}(j,j_N):\mathbb{Q}(j)] = \psi(N)$, equivalently of the irreducibility of the modular polynomial $\Phi_N$ over $\mathbb{Q}(j)$, at prime-square times prime levels.
